Change to harness/wspagent_settings.json (M5); applied to the repo in 29ebbf1. Install it yourself as below.

Why:
- On Linux/WSL2, Claude Code ignores sandbox.network.allowUnixSockets (macOS only). The seccomp filter blocks every
  AF_UNIX socket unless sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets is true, so fp_query/wsp_submit could not reach
  /run/wsp/fp.sock from the sandboxed Bash tool. The allowUnixSockets list is kept for macOS parity (JSON has no comments).
- allowAllUnixSockets also reopens the WSL interop socket (cmd.exe, powershell.exe). The Bash deny rules below are a
  speed bump only (full paths or `sh -c` bypass prefix rules). The real control is interop disabled in /etc/wsl.conf during
  batches, plus audit.py marking any *.exe, /mnt/<drive> or wslpath use as invalid.
- Read(//home/MAINUSER/**) was a placeholder; with the literal name the rule matches nothing. Drop that hunk if your
  installed copy is already substituted. chmod 700 /home/mainuser is the primary control either way.

Apply + install:
  cd ~/repo && patch -p1 < harness/wspagent_settings.diff
  sudo chattr -i /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json 2>/dev/null   # required before any update (immutable bit)
  sudo install -o root -g wspagent -m 640 harness/wspagent_settings.json /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json
  sudo chattr +i /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json
  (root-owned and immutable so wspagent can neither edit nor replace it; make_run's preflight.sh fails otherwise)
  sudo sha256sum /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json && sha256sum harness/wspagent_settings.json   # must match
Interop off for batches (/etc/wsl.conf), then from Windows: wsl --shutdown   (this also empties /run/wsp):
  [interop]
  enabled=false
  appendWindowsPath=false
Then commit the patched harness/wspagent_settings.json; audit.py compares installed settings against it.

